WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.626 --> 00:00:03.044
When I think about being on stage

00:00:03.044 --> 00:00:03.920
and performing,

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:06.214
first thing that comes to my mind is...

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:08.049
intensity.

00:00:08.633 --> 00:00:10.427
When Run was being Run,

00:00:10.719 --> 00:00:12.095
Darryl was being Darryl,

00:00:12.095 --> 00:00:13.888
and Jay was being Jay,

00:00:13.888 --> 00:00:14.764
it was heaven.

00:00:14.764 --> 00:00:15.974
It was Nirvana.

00:00:16.266 --> 00:00:17.142
When we get on stage

00:00:17.142 --> 00:00:18.184
we do what we gotta do.

00:00:19.269 --> 00:00:20.186
Rock the house.

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:23.023
Party people.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:26.109
Your dreams have now been fulfilled.

00:00:27.277 --> 00:00:28.486
Hollis, Queens.

00:00:32.741 --> 00:00:33.575
Hold up.

00:00:33.992 --> 00:00:34.909
Let’s back up.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:37.412
My reason for getting into rap

00:00:37.412 --> 00:00:38.705
was the streets.

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:40.415
Everybody in the neighborhood

00:00:40.415 --> 00:00:42.375
started getting two turntables and a mixer.

00:00:42.751 --> 00:00:44.127
At this point, me and D,

00:00:44.127 --> 00:00:45.003
we were dreaming about

00:00:45.003 --> 00:00:46.212
making our own stuff.

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:47.172
Grab your rhyme book.

00:00:47.172 --> 00:00:48.465
We’re going to the studio

00:00:48.465 --> 00:00:49.257
to make a record.

00:00:49.257 --> 00:00:49.841
♪ Here we go ♪

00:00:50.592 --> 00:00:52.177
That was the moment I knew

00:00:52.177 --> 00:00:53.803
hip-hop was gonna be huge.

00:00:53.803 --> 00:00:55.555
They brought more people to the genre.

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:57.348
♪ Tricky Tricky Tricky Tricky ♪

00:00:57.766 --> 00:00:59.642
All this from two turntables

00:00:59.642 --> 00:01:00.477
and a microphone.

00:01:01.186 --> 00:01:01.978
Now that it’s a hit

00:01:01.978 --> 00:01:03.855
you gotta go perform it in front of people.

00:01:03.855 --> 00:01:05.023
We exploded out of nowhere.

00:01:05.315 --> 00:01:07.025
It was so big it overtook us.

00:01:07.942 --> 00:01:09.444
What defines greatness

00:01:09.444 --> 00:01:10.779
is how you react

00:01:10.779 --> 00:01:12.572
when things aren’t going great.

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:13.364
D!

00:01:13.364 --> 00:01:14.324
Open the door!

00:01:14.324 --> 00:01:15.658
I wasn’t dealing with

00:01:15.658 --> 00:01:17.368
the feelings and the emotions

00:01:17.368 --> 00:01:18.453
that I was going through.

00:01:18.453 --> 00:01:20.163
I was just ready to give up.

00:01:20.168 --> 00:01:21.748
After that, all hell broke loose.

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:23.833
Run DMC is officially retired.

00:01:24.709 --> 00:01:25.752
It made him go...

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:26.878
This is who we are.

00:01:26.878 --> 00:01:28.338
And we ain’t from The Bronx.

00:01:28.338 --> 00:01:29.422
And we ain’t from Brooklyn.

00:01:30.131 --> 00:01:31.174
We from Queens!

00:01:32.717 --> 00:01:33.426
They made something

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:34.594
that no one ever made before.

00:01:35.386 --> 00:01:36.805
They the reason hip-hop is as

00:01:36.805 --> 00:01:38.223
big as it is right now.

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:42.352
I did not know until the last second

00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:44.312
that I was about to go do something

00:01:44.312 --> 00:01:45.897
so big and so historic.

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:48.316
They changed the sound of music,

00:01:48.316 --> 00:01:50.652
the audience for rap music.

00:01:50.652 --> 00:01:52.153
When you saw me, Run, and Jay,

00:01:52.153 --> 00:01:53.863
you didn’t see celebrity.

00:01:55.288 --> 00:01:56.414
You saw yourself.

00:01:57.511 --> 00:01:58.637
You get in front of the world...

00:01:59.584 --> 00:02:01.859
and you let people know who you are.

